{
  "description": "Page Mollie's list operations, which the converter's detection does not recognise. Every list takes `from` (\"Provide an ID to start the result set from the item with the given ID and onwards. This allows you to paginate the result set.\") and `limit`, and returns the items under `_embedded.<resource>` beside HAL `_links`, whose `next` is the URL of the next page (with its `from` query value) or null on the last page. Read off the spec's parameter descriptions and the `next` link in its list examples (e.g. list-refunds-200-1: `.../refunds?from=re_APBiGPH2vV&limit=5`). The business-account lists take `from` too but document no `_links`, so they stay single-page.",
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/shapes/com.mollie#ListBalances/traits/smithy.api#paginated",
      "value": {
        "mode": "cursor",
        "inputToken": "from",
        "outputToken": "_links.next.href",
        "items": "_embedded.balances",
        "pageSize": "limit"
      }
